                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="1771-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_c.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Cardioid" title="Cardioid" ></span>Lewitt Audio LCT 240 PRO</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Cardioid Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The LCT 240 PRO is a scaled-down version of Lewitt&#8217;s LCT 240, lacking all switches such as pad, low cut, and Lewitt&#8217;s clipping history feature. Removing these features makes the 240 PRO less expensive and it is thus the new entry microphone in Lewitt&#8217;s LCT line.</p><p>The mic has a different capsule than the more expensive mics in the line. It is not a full 25.4 (1&#8221;) diaphragm, though the physical design does resemble the large-diaphragm mics in Lewitt&#8217;s product line. </p><p>Instead, the 240 PRO shares the same 17mm small-diaphragm electret capsule as the 240, which in turn shares its capsule with the LCT 140, Lewitt&#8217;s entry-level pencil microphone. However, the vastly different body shapes, different amplifier designs (though all employ transformerless circuits with surface-mount components) and the more open headbasket of the 240/240 PRO mean the 140 and 240/240 PRO are very different mics, despite the shared capsule.</p><p>Technical specifications bear out that the mic seems best suited for bedroom recording of vocals and acoustic guitars: it has quite a pronounced top end with a substantial peak at 8kHz, and the low end begins to roll off starting at 100Hz, thus decreasing the need for a low cut filter. The microphone can handle high SPL, however - 142db - so it can be used for instruments and amplifiers. Lewitt&#8217;s marketing materials give some idea of the mic&#8217;s purpose as an entry-level all-rounder: &#8216;Record&#8217;, it says.</p><p>Unique to Lewitt&#8217;s LCT line, the 240 PRO comes in white as well as black.</p><p>The package includes a rubber swivel mount, a leatherette mic bag, and a foam windscreen.<p>Permalink: <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Lewitt/LCT240PRO">Lewitt Audio LCT240PRO</a></p><p>The mic was released in 2016.</p>
